Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/view/View.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), the
platform Toolbar's step (the platform action bar): View.getWindowId() of a window that has no window session.

Why: AOSP asks the window session for the window's WindowId, and Minato's windows have none (ADR-0041), so the call is a
NullPointerException. TransitionManager's pre-draw listener calls it (Transition.playTransition), which every popup and
menu that animates through a transition reaches. What changes: a window without a session answers null, which Transition
compares by identity, so the views of the one window still match each other.

--- a/core/java/android/view/View.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/View.java
@@ -22747,6 +22747,11 @@
         if (ai == null) {
             return null;
         }
+        if (ai.mSession == null) {
+            // Minato's windows have no window session (ADR-0041), so no window ID: the one every view of the window
+            // answers, which is how Transition tells the views of one window apart.
+            return null;
+        }
         if (ai.mWindowId == null) {
             try {
                 ai.mIWindowId = ai.mSession.getWindowId(ai.mWindowToken);
